# Czar public alpha: the credential files czar-secrets.service writes at boot (SCR-170 §4).
#
# This file holds NAMES ONLY. No value of any kind belongs here, ever. Each row says which
# Secret Manager secret to read and where its bytes land under deploy.credentialFilesDir
# (/run/czar/secrets), which UID may read the file, and whether the boot may continue without it.
#
# Columns:
#   secret        the Secret Manager secret, always under the czar-alpha-* prefix the VM's
#                 service account is granted roles/secretmanager.secretAccessor on
#   service       the subfolder, which is the only folder that service's container sees
#   file          the file name inside that subfolder, as the config key names it
#   uid           the container UID that reads it: 10002 for the signer, 10001 for every other
#                 Czar image, 0 for root-only files (SCR-170 §4)
#   requirement   required  -> a missing secret stops the boot
#                 optional  -> a missing secret is skipped, because the feature is off by default
#
# Two rows may name the same secret: a signer client reads its token from its own folder, and
# the signer reads the same value as its expected token for that client. One secret, one value,
# two destinations.
#
# secret                              service    file                    uid    requirement

# Per-role database passwords (SCR-170 §5). The connection URL never carries a password.
czar-alpha-db-password-server         server     db-password             10001  required
czar-alpha-db-password-signer         signer     db-password             10002  required
czar-alpha-db-password-indexer        indexer    db-password             10001  required
czar-alpha-db-password-merchants      merchants  db-password             10001  required
czar-alpha-db-password-backup         backup     db-password             0      required

# Signer socket tokens (SCR-170 §4). The client reads its own token; the signer reads the
# expected token for each client under signer/client-tokens/<service>.
czar-alpha-signer-token-server        server     signer-token            10001  required
czar-alpha-signer-token-server        signer     client-tokens/server    10002  required
czar-alpha-signer-token-merchants     merchants  signer-token            10001  required
czar-alpha-signer-token-merchants     signer     client-tokens/merchants 10002  required

# The model provider (SCR-170 §6). models.provider defaults to none and the first live run needs
# Zaryab's approval, so this one is optional: until he connects a provider the secret has no
# version and the boot carries on without the file.
czar-alpha-anthropic-api-key          server     anthropic-api-key       10001  optional
